 Honey, and Paidy names. The company was founded in 1998 and is headquartered in San Jose, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Enrique J. Lores | President, CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $167,534 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 23K people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 14%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $234K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $42K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["PayPal Holdings, Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $49.2B market cap on $33.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $5.6B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.23\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 14\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 12.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 35% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 23% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Financial Services peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"PayPal (NASDAQ:PYPL) Shares Up 3.4% \u2013 Should You Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/paypal-nasdaqpypl-shares-up-3-4-should-you-buy.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794013374.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.