ransaction_type":"exercise","shares":2910.0,"price_per_share":0.0,"dollar_value":0.0,"shares_after":92537.0}],"_trap_components":{"decline":{"score":0.0,"weight":0.25},"balance_sheet":{"score":0.167,"weight":0.2},"value_destruction":{"score":0.0,"weight":0.2},"derating":{"score":0.5,"weight":0.15},"market":{"score":0.0,"weight":0.1}},"data_summaries":{"sect":["Its 18% operating margin trails the Financial Services median (29%) by 11pp, so it is a below-average operator in its field.","It earns less of the sector's profit than its revenue share would suggest (0.71x).","It accounts for 0.8% of sector revenue and 0.6% of sector operating profit.","Over five years it has been gaining share of the sector profit pool (+1.1% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.02 across 512 companies in the universe; the top four hold 20% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares have drifted lower, down 17% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 13% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 42% and a beta of 1.25, it amplifies market moves, though its beta has shifted (1y 0.48 vs 5y 1.36), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $578.4M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 31% in the 2020 crash and 65% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The stock trades 35% below its DCF fair value of $90.58, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 10%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $73.06 to $116 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks cheap against Financial Services peers: EV/EBITDA 8.1 vs 10.9 and P/FCF 8.8 vs 12.9 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 67% below its 10-year median.","The 33 covering analysts target $56.83 on average, 4% below the price, well away from the model's fair value.","The price implies 3.4% annual cash-flow growth, 8pp less than the model expects."],"prof":["ROIC of 22% clears the cost of capital of 9.7% by 13pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have been steady (CV 0.25).","It converts 17% of revenue into free cash flow.","It earns a 26% return on equity."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 6.4% over 3 years, 9.1% over 5 years and 13.6% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 10% of profits supports about 2.2% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 5.0% on average.","Analysts expect 5.8% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.7%), and institutions hold 81%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (12 sales, net $889K sold).","It returns 12.3% a year to shareholders (12.1% in buybacks and 0.9% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 6.4% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 23,800 employees, each generates about $1.4M of revenue, 2.8x the Financial Services median, and productivity has risen 13.6% a year.","That works out to $234K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $168K (0x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $42K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":83,"head":"Watch: no strong case either way.","pros":["Trades 35% below fair value of $90.58","ROE 25.8% vs cost of equity 10.9%","Revenue grew 9.1%/yr over 5y","Piotroski F-score 7/9","EV/EBITDA 8.1x vs sector 10.9x"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":["the model rates it HOLD"],"buy_below":76.99,"vc":{"base":90.58,"base_src":"dcf","bear":73.06,"bull":115.85,"alt_median":73.3,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.2357,"dispersion":0.1039,"level":"HIGH","why":[]},"med":{"pe":12.155,"ev_ebitda":10.862,"pfcf":12.9041,"pb":1.3934,"roic":0.116,"gross_margin":0.4181,"fcf_margin":0.2507,"div_yield":0.0265}},"ticker":"PYPL","date":"2026-11-06"}